# frules precedence

When several Forth rules are in context (Cursor attaches whole `.mdc` files by `globs`; cross-references do not auto-load), apply this order on conflict:

1. **`frules-dialect.mdc`** — chosen dialect (always applied).
2. **`forth-system-context.mdc`** — route **system/architecture** questions vs **code/challenge** tasks (always applied).
3. **`forth-dialect-<name>.mdc`** — dialect syntax and idioms.
4. **`forth-portability.mdc`** — only when the project targets multiple Forths.
5. **`forth-anti-patterns.mdc`** — fix violations before adding more code.
6. **Other `forth-*.mdc`** — generic guidance (stack, style, control, factoring, defining, memory, io, strings, numeric, wordlists, debugging, oof, c-bindings, floating-point, meta).

Topic routing (pick the most specific file for the task):

| Task | Rule file |
|------|-----------|
| **System / niche / architecture** (FMAP, threading, layers, co-design, FORTH-X, choosing a Forth) | `forth-system-context.mdc` → linked `docs/FORTH-*.md` |
| **Implement or fix Forth code** (challenges, `.fs`, stack effects) | `forth-stack`, `forth-style`, `forth-control`, … — **not** architecture docs unless porting |
| Stack order, manipulation, stack-effect design | `forth-stack.mdc` |
| Typing model (no type check, stack contract) | `forth-stack.mdc` |
| Cell size, portable numeric range, multi-target deps | `forth-portability.mdc` |
| Double/mixed precision, pictured numeric output | `forth-numeric.mdc` |
| if/loop/exit/recursion/flags, extended case | `forth-control.mdc` |
| Challenge debug / `T{ }T` (train solve done; validate on `eval_holdout`) | `docs/AGENT-SOLVE-CHALLENGES.md` §5b + `forth-control.mdc` |
| Rosetta Code snippet hints for a bank task | `sources/rosettacode-forth/INDEX.md` + `python3 scripts/rosettacode-hint.py <challenge.fs>` |
| CREATE/DOES>, defer, quotations, forward, alias | `forth-defining.mdc` |
| immediate, postpone, `[`/`]`, parsing/recognizers | `forth-meta.mdc` |
| variable, create, allot, move/cmove, alignment | `forth-memory.mdc` |
| `create` name + hyphenated word (Gforth tokenizer) | `forth-naming.mdc` § Hyphens vs create |
| Indexed `ch@`/`ch!`, parallel array “lists” | `forth-memory.mdc` § Indexed buffers |
| Singly-linked list nodes, `bounds` | `forth-memory.mdc` § Singly-linked lists |
| +field struct layout, queue defining word | `forth-defining.mdc` § Field offsets |
| MODULE/EXPORT modules | `forth-wordlists.mdc` § MODULE |
| Auxiliary cell stack (not return stack) | `forth-stack.mdc` § Auxiliary cell stacks |
| String stack (`"push`/`"pop`) | `forth-strings.mdc` § String stack |
| Fixed-point `places`/`fixed` (one cell) | `forth-numeric.mdc` § Fixed-point |
| `[IMMEDIATE]` early marker, interpretive wordlist | `forth-meta.mdc` |
| Challenge solution vs scaffold stubs (`redefined`) | `forth-dialect-gforth.mdc` § Challenge solution copies |
| Hold pointer across helpers (`variable`) | `forth-factoring.mdc` § variable as handle |
| open-file, CLI args, search paths | `forth-io.mdc` |
| s", c-addr u, xchars | `forth-strings.mdc` |
| FP stack, 1e, f~abs | `forth-floating-point.mdc` |
| Word lists, vocabularies, search order | `forth-wordlists.mdc` |
| see, ~~, depth-changes, inspection | `forth-debugging.mdc` |
| objects.fs classes (optional OOP) | `forth-oof.mdc` |
| cfunction, calling C libraries | `forth-c-bindings.mdc` |
| Gforth locals, require, try/endtry, structs | `forth-dialect-gforth.mdc` |
| FORTH architecture docs (human reference) | `docs/FORTH-*-eng.md` (English) or `docs/FORTH-*.md` (Russian) |
| Custom hardware / FPGA co-design with Forth | `docs/FORTH-HARDWARE-CODESIGN.md` (human reference) |
| Choosing Forth system for a project / domain | `docs/FORTH-FMAP-GUIDE.md` (human reference) |
| Threading models (ITC/DTC/STC), colon body format | `docs/FORTH-THREADING.md` (human reference) |
| Embedded port, system architecture, FMAP/FTAS | `docs/FORTH-SYSTEM-ARCHITECTURE.md` (human reference) |
| Superscalar stack CPU research (Elbrus, zzeng) | `docs/FORTH-STACK-CPU-RESEARCH-eng.md` / `docs/FORTH-STACK-CPU-RESEARCH.md` (human reference) |
| Embedded port, missing wordsets, feature cost | `docs/FORTH-FEATURE-COMPLEXITY.md` (human reference) |
| Domain dialects FORTH-X, layer 0 | `docs/FORTH-DIALECT-LAYERS.md` (human reference) |
| Route architecture vs coding tasks | `forth-system-context.mdc` |

Do not repeat stack-tutorial material inside a defining-word edit.

If a needed topic is missing, prefer portable ANS words and ask to add `rules/forth-<topic>.mdc` from `sources/` (e.g. `gforth-manual/`, `gforth-manual-tutorial/`, `brodie-thinking-forth/`, `rosettacode-forth/`).
